  "details": "1. Enter any instance, any world.  \n\n2. Open Quick Menu.\n\n3. Observe frame stuttering and mismatched frames between eyes.\n\nHaving players behind the Quick Menu seems to help it occurs more frequently in my experience, and sometimes this occurs without the quick menu open, opening the Quick Menu only seems to make it more frequent for whatever reason.\n\nI do not know if my hardware configuration is at fault, so I will list my parts.  I have talked to friends, and they seem to experience this issue even on nVidia hardware, so I do not think this an AMD specific issue.  This issue does not occur on Mainline Unity 2019 version of VRChat for me.  I tried to record a video with OBS, and I cannot show the full extent of the issue without showing both VR eyes captured  (will try to find a way to capture both eyes).\n\nThis seems to happen when specific avatars load, or I go to specific worlds... but it is difficult to reproduce so I do not have more details at this time.  This bug gives me a headache and makes VRChat unplayable in VR.\n\nCPU: AMD Ryzen 9 5950x\n\nRAM: 32GBs DDR4-3600\n\nGPU: AMD Radeon 6800 XT\n\nMotherboard: ASRock X470 Taichi\n\nHMD: HP Reverb G2\n\nControllers: Valve Knuckles (HTC branded 2.0 base stations).\n\nFBT: 4x HTC Vive 2.0 Trackers (one set for continuous tracking on forehead using forked version of SpaceCAL)",
